  "lineage": "Hereditary oral-history and praise practice of the jeli, gewel and gawlo castes across Mali, Guinea, Senegal, the Gambia and Burkina Faso, attributed in tradition to Bala Faseke Kouyaté at the thirteenth-century court of Sunjata Keita — free-tempo genealogical recitation (sataro) alternating with sung fasa melody in high strained tessitura over a fixed kumbengo ostinato on kora, ngoni or balafon, with heavy melisma, patron-naming interjection and no fixed piece length.",
